</section>

<section class="pipeline-section" id="alerts"><div class="shell"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">How it works</p><h2>Scan now,<br>then keep measuring.</h2><p>A scan fetches the page once, runs the technical, SEO, performance, and content analyzers, and looks for analytics tools in the markup. The HTTP check and certificate read are the same ones the scheduler runs. Everything is stored as events, so a domain scanned today has a history next month.</p></div>
<ol class="engine-path" aria-label="Flow">{% for step in ["Domain","HTTP + SSL check","Analyzers","Analytics detection","Snapshot event","Scheduled checks"] %}<li><span class="project-type">{{ loop.index0 | pad }}</span><strong>{{ step }}</strong></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
<pre class="vector-console" aria-label="Rules">IF the check fails or returns 5xx      THEN status = unavailable → incident
IF status is 4xx or response &gt; 1500 ms  THEN status = degraded → warning
IF the certificate expires within 14 days THEN ssl warning
IF status returns to operational         THEN recovered</pre>
<p class="fine-print">The analytics score reflects which tracking tools the page loads. Signal does not read any analytics account; traffic figures would need Search Console or GA access and are not shown. Scores use Vector's documented scoring.</p></div></section>
